Hegseth's latest shake-up reportedly targets seven more Army officers who had been selected for promotion to two-star general, while the broader cuts have already hit roughly 10% of the military's top officers. And now Army Secretary Dan Driscoll is out amid the turmoil.

There are legitimate reasons to replace senior officers. There are legitimate reasons to reform the Pentagon. But when the departures keep piling up and professional disagreement starts looking suspiciously like a fucking career-ending condition, eventually you've got to ask what you're building:

